# Campora environment variables — copy to .env.local and fill in real values.
# NEVER commit .env.local or real secrets.
#
# Both variables are REQUIRED for the full-stack version (login, profiles,
# posts). You can find them in the Supabase dashboard under
# Project Settings -> API. They are public client credentials: the anon key
# is safe to use in the browser because Row Level Security policies
# (supabase/schema.sql) protect the data. Never put the secret service-role
# key in this file or anywhere in the frontend.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
